{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_028 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, resnet50, concat) achieved 42.7% accuracy, which is modest and suggests a bottleneck in one of the modalities. Uncertainty: it's unclear whether the image encoder (ResNet50) is a limiting factor compared to the RNA encoder or fusion strategy. This experiment (config_002) is a clean A/B test that changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings identical (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, no aggregation, concat fusion). ViT-L is a substantially stronger image backbone, so this directly tests whether image representation quality is the primary bottleneck. If accuracy improves meaningfully, we gain a strong direction to exploit in remaining experiments (e.g., adding multiprofile/transformer aggregation on top of ViT-L). If it does not improve, we learn the image modality is not the bottleneck and should pivot to RNA encoder or fusion strategy. With 8 experiments remaining, this single-variable test maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design axis before committing to further structural changes."
}

